Hi,

> I want to contribute code to support audio codec Philips UDA1380.
> Download from: "http://www.mandarinlogiq.org/PXA2xx i2Sound/"
> 
This URL is broken and needs to be fixed. :)
s/ /%20/

> Clean write for ALSA and kernel 2.6 with full power optimizations at subchip 
> level, enabling hw blocks on need. Looking around in the kernel, this seems 
> to be a novelty among sound drivers, that run commonly in an 
> all-always-powered-up manner.
> 
Is there any reason why you didn't use the pxa2xx-pcm code
(sound/arm/pxa2xx-pcm.c) which is already working perfectly with AC97
and can be used for I2S without any change.

Some comments on your code (see attached patch):
- The register cache for the UDA1380 is defined in uda1380.h as 0x24
  words in size, but the highest register number accessed is 0x28,
  which makes up for a perfect buffer overflow due to missing array
  bounds checking.
- The cache flush routines unecessarily always write registers from
  the start of a section instead of flushing only registers that have
  really been modified.
- The INV_RANGE() macro is off by one.
- __BIG_ENDIAN is undefined on little endian machines, thus
  '#if __BIG_ENDIAN' gives a compiler warning.
- The macro 'flag_stream()' in pxa2xx-i2sound.c is missing parentheses
  around the expression
- There are lots of bogus spaces or tabs at line endings.


Lothar Wassmann

--faT63KuFhO
